\caption(Observed binary outcomes and fitted probabilities by site, with the common zero-effect reference.)
\alttext(Observed binary outcomes and fitted probabilities by site, with the common zero-effect reference.)

> Interpretation

The random-effect penalty shrinks each site intercept toward zero while
the smooth is shared. The fit uses supplied smoothing penalties and a
supplied random-intercept SD. The zero-effect curve evaluates the response
at group effect zero. It does not average the inverse logit over the
random-effect distribution.

> References

- [Eilers and Marx, Flexible smoothing with B-splines and penalties|https://doi.org/10.1214/ss/1038425655]
- [mgcv random-effects documentation|https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/mgcv/html/random.effects.html]
